From dbec44ce47b89d53f275ea7f187a48ac88e567c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vinay Adella <vadella@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 11:42:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] iw: add band-based channel selection for scan commands

Without this change, scanning a specific band requires the user
to enumerate every frequency manually. Add a 'band 2g|5g|6g'
token to 'iw scan', 'iw scan trigger', and 'iw scan sched_start'
that automatically resolves all active channels for the requested
band by querying NL80211_CMD_GET_WIPHY and populating
NL80211_ATTR_SCAN_FREQUENCIES accordingly.

New helper get_band_freqs() in util.c issues a GET_WIPHY request
for the interface, walks NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY_BANDS for the target
band index, and skips any frequency marked
NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_DISABLED.

parse_sched_scan() is extended with state/ifindex parameters so
the same band resolution is available for scheduled scans and
WoWLAN net-detect triggers.

Example usage:
  iw dev wlan0 scan band 5g
  iw dev wlan0 scan trigger band 6g
  iw dev wlan0 scan sched_start interval 30000 band 2g

Signed-off-by: Vinay Adella <vadella@qti.qualcomm.com>
